public class DangerousApp {
    public void deleteSystemFiles() {
        File file = new File("C:/Windows/System32");
        file.delete();  // Not allowed in sandbox!
    }
}
If run in a sandbox, this code will fail due to the SecurityManager rejecting the file delete operation.

🔐 Modern Use
Applets are deprecated, but the concept of sandboxing is still relevant in:

JVM-based web servers

Cloud-based execution environments

Java-based plugin systems

Spring Security and containers like Docker also apply sandboxing in broader forms.

